### Registration

Competitors interested in participating in **pkmn.ai**'s ladders or tournaments
can request inclusion [via GitHub](TODO). You will be required to provide:

    - your project's **name** (subject to staff discretion, prefer regex `^[A-Za-Z
    ]$`, must not include the tokens `poke` / `mon` / `pkmn` / `AI` / `bot` /
    `agent` / `showdown` / `smogon`, bare English Pokémon species names, or
    known player's names)
    - **GitHub and Smogon usernames** for each team member associated with your
    project. All authorized team members must be Smogon account holders in good
    standing.
    - descriptive fields on **project details** for the [projects](/projects)
    page - agreement to follow [Responsible Release](/release) guidelines and to
    grant **pkmn.ai** permission to run your code in its arena for the purpose
    of evaluation against other agents and for evaluating suspected cheating
    cases in Smogon & Pokémon Showdown competitions
    - **Discord user IDs** (_optional_) of the team members, to be used for
    notifications about your submissions and for roles within the
    [chat](/chat) room
    - A PNG image (_optional_) with your project's **logo** to be displayed on
    your project's statistics page


This will open up an issue on the [pkmn/ai](https://github.com/pkmn/ai)
repository. Staff will review this issue, fill in the approriate information in
the [`projects.yml`](https://github.com/pkmn/ai/blob/main/static/projects.yml),
and approve your project for submissions.

### Submission

Approved competitors may submit new versions of their agent via the
[submissions](/submit) page which requires GitHub OAuth credentials to
authenticate. On this page you will be required to fill in:

  - **`version`**: Version string (e.g., `1.0.0` or `v2`, regex
  `^[A-Za-z0-9._-]{1,24}$`).
  - **`download_url`**: Direct HTTPS URL to a `.tar.gz`/`tar.xz`/`.tar.zst` bundle
  _or_ an OCI container image reference (`ghcr.io/...`, `docker.io/...`).
  - **`sha256`**: 64-character hex SHA-256 checksum of the archive or OCI manifest
  digest.
  - (_optional_) **`auth_token`**: Read-only bearer token / header used once by the
  arena to pull private artifacts
  - **`ladders`**: / **`tournaments`**: non-empty subsets of the ladders or tournaments
  to enter your agent in

Ladder submissions will run on a **Mac M6 Mini** with access to **10 cores** (8
Performance & 2 Efficiency), **14 GiB** of dedicated RAM and 4 GiB of scratch
`/tmp` storage wiped between games. The **network will be disabled** for all
competitors. Ladder submissions may either take the form of an OCI `linux/arm64`
Container which can access the GPU virtually via Vulkan passthrough or a native
bundle that has full native access to the GPU/ANE Metal/CoreML. Tournament
hardware will be outlined in the tournament-specific rules and will only support
OCI containers.

{summary="**OCI Container**"}
::: details
```dockerfile
FROM --platform=linux/arm64 rust:1.85-slim AS builder
WORKDIR /src
COPY . .
RUN cargo build --release && strip --strip-unneeded target/release/my-bot

FROM --platform=linux/arm64 debian:bookworm-slim
COPY --from=builder /src/target/release/my-bot /usr/local/bin/my-bot
ENTRYPOINT ["/usr/local/bin/my-bot"]
```
:::

{summary="**Native Bundle**"}
::: details
```bash
mkdir -p dist/src dist/weights
uv python install 3.12
uv venv --python 3.12 --relocatable --no-cache dist/.venv
uv pip install --no-cache --python dist/.venv/bin/python mlx numpy
find dist/.venv -name '__pycache__' -type d -exec rm -rf {} +

cp src/*.py dist/src/
cp weights/*.safetensors dist/weights/

cat << 'EOF' > dist/run
#!/usr/bin/env bash
DIR="$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)"
exec "${DIR}/.venv/bin/python" -u "${DIR}/src/main.py" --weights "${DIR}/weights"
EOF
chmod +x dist/run
tar -czf bot-bundle.tar.gz -C dist .
```
:::

Every bot submission must occupy at most **500 MB of uncompressed resident
space** on disk once unpacked. Native bundles must contain less than 25,000
files/directories/symlinks and contain an executable `./run` at the archive
root. OCI Containers must contain less than 32 OCI layers and the container
`ENTRYPOINT` / `CMD` must run the agent.

Tournaments will accept only the first successful entry for a project. Ladder
competitors may have up to 2 versions of their project competing concurrently
though may only submit a new version of their bot after both of the following
conditions are true:

  - 14 days has elapsed since their last successful ladder submission
  - all of their previous submissions have settled to $`\text{SE}(R) \le
  30\text{ Elo}` ($`\hat{\sigma} \le 0.173` nats, 95% CI $`\approx \pm 59\text{
  Elo}`) and at least 25 blind-pair matches (50 games)

A submission is determined to be successful if the the arena can successfully
unpack and play through the first turn of a battle in the format(s) it is
entered in. For ladder submissions, if there are already 2 versions of a project
on the same ladder the weaker of the two versions for that format's ladder will
be automatically retired, leaving the strongest version of the agent and the
latest submission.

